    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d346-a1">

                <pb facs="0460" n="372" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg372"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Messrs. C. Lyon Hall &amp;
                            Co. to Mr. Battiste.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-09-10"><hi rendition="#italic">September 10,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: We beg to call your attention to the law
                    published in the Moniteur of 22 August, 1903, putting an extra tax on foreigners
                    doing business in Haiti, <hi rendition="#italic">in articles Nos. 55 to 71 and
                        especially in article 63</hi>, which fixes the amount at half the tax
                    already paid for our “patents.”</p>
                <p>This tax is not imposed on Haitiens, only on foreigners, and we consider it in
                    violation of the treaty in force between the United States and Haiti and ought
                    not to be imposed on American firms.</p>
                <p>Hoping that this matter may be satisfactorily arranged, we have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">C. Lyon Hall</hi> &amp; Co.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
